---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../css/legal.css';

const updated = 'September 2026';
const sections = [
  { id: 'who-we-are',        t: 'Who we are' },
  { id: 'information',       t: 'Information we collect' },
  { id: 'how-we-use',        t: 'How we use information' },
  { id: 'legal-basis',       t: 'Sharing & disclosure' },
  { id: 'cookies',           t: 'Cookies & tracking' },
  { id: 'storage',           t: 'Data storage & security' },
  { id: 'retention',         t: 'Data retention' },
  { id: 'your-rights',       t: 'Your rights' },
  { id: 'third-parties',     t: 'Third-party services' },
  { id: 'children',          t: 'Children’s privacy' },
  { id: 'changes',           t: 'Changes to this policy' },
  { id: 'contact',           t: 'Contact us' },
];
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy — AccrualOS"
  description="How AccrualOS collects, uses and protects your information, in line with the Australian Privacy Principles."
>
<main class="lg">

  <!-- HERO -->
  <header class="lg-hero">
    <div class="lg-hero-in">
      <nav class="lg-crumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span>Privacy Policy</nav>
      <span class="lg-eyebrow">Legal</span>
      <h1 class="lg-h1">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="lg-updated">Last updated: <b>{updated}</b></p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <div class="lg-wrap">

    <!-- TOC -->
    <nav class="lg-toc" aria-label="On this page">
      <p class="lg-toc-title">On this page</p>
      <ol>
        {sections.map((s) => <li><a href={`#${s.id}`}>{s.t}</a></li>)}
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <!-- BODY -->
    <div class="lg-body">
      <p class="lg-intro">AccrualOS ("AccrualOS", "we", "us" or "our") is committed to protecting the privacy of the accounting and bookkeeping practices, their team members, and their clients who use our platform. This Privacy Policy explains what information we collect, how we use it, and the choices you have. It is written to be consistent with the Australian Privacy Principles (APPs) under the <i>Privacy Act 1988</i> (Cth).</p>

      <div class="lg-note"><b>Note:</b> This document is a general template. It should be reviewed by a qualified legal adviser and tailored to your registered entity, ABN, and actual data practices before you rely on it.</div>

      <h2 id="who-we-are"><span class="n">01</span>Who we are</h2>
      <p>AccrualOS is a practice-management and automation platform built for Australian accounting and bookkeeping firms. The platform is developed and operated within the Sharktech Global technology group and runs on the VCPility automation engine. Where this policy refers to a "data controller", it refers to the AccrualOS operating entity.</p>

      <h2 id="information"><span class="n">02</span>Information we collect</h2>
      <p>We collect information in the following ways:</p>
      <h3>Information you provide</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Account and contact details — name, business name, email address, phone number, and role.</li>
        <li>Billing details required to process your subscription (handled by our payment provider).</li>
        <li>Content you enter into the platform, including client records, enquiries, documents, messages, and workflow data.</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Information collected automatically</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Usage data such as pages viewed, features used, and actions taken within the platform.</li>
        <li>Device and connection data such as IP address, browser type, and operating system.</li>
        <li>Cookies and similar technologies (see <a href="#cookies">Cookies &amp; tracking</a>).</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="how-we-use"><span class="n">03</span>How we use information</h2>
      <p>We use the information we collect to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Provide, operate, and maintain the AccrualOS platform and its features.</li>
        <li>Process your subscription, send service communications, and provide support.</li>
        <li>Run the automations you configure, such as reminders, follow-ups, and booking confirmations.</li>
        <li>Improve, secure, and troubleshoot the platform.</li>
        <li>Comply with our legal and regulatory obligations.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="legal-basis"><span class="n">04</span>Sharing &amp; disclosure</h2>
      <p>We do not sell your personal information. We may share information only in these circumstances:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><b>Service providers</b> who help us run the platform (for example hosting, email delivery, and payment processing), bound by confidentiality obligations.</li>
        <li><b>Within our group</b> (Sharktech Global / VCPility) where necessary to deliver and support the service.</li>
        <li><b>Legal requirements</b> — where disclosure is required by law, court order, or to protect rights, safety, and property.</li>
        <li><b>Business transfers</b> — in connection with a merger, acquisition, or sale of assets, subject to this policy.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="cookies"><span class="n">05</span>Cookies &amp; tracking</h2>
      <p>We use cookies and similar technologies to keep you signed in, remember your preferences, and understand how the platform is used. You can control cookies through your browser settings; disabling some cookies may affect how the platform works.</p>

      <h2 id="storage"><span class="n">06</span>Data storage &amp; security</h2>
      <p>We take reasonable technical and organisational measures to protect your information against loss, misuse, and unauthorised access, including encryption in transit, access controls, and monitoring. Wherever practicable, client data for Australian practices is hosted in Australia. No method of transmission or storage is completely secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.</p>

      <h2 id="retention"><span class="n">07</span>Data retention</h2>
      <p>We retain personal information for as long as your account is active and for a reasonable period afterwards to meet legal, accounting, and reporting obligations. When information is no longer required, we take steps to delete or de-identify it.</p>

      <h2 id="your-rights"><span class="n">08</span>Your rights</h2>
      <p>Subject to applicable law, you may request to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Access the personal information we hold about you.</li>
        <li>Correct information that is inaccurate or out of date.</li>
        <li>Request deletion of your information where we are not required to keep it.</li>
        <li>Withdraw consent or object to certain processing.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>To exercise any of these rights, contact us using the details below. You may also lodge a complaint with the Office of the Australian Information Commissioner (OAIC) at <a href="https://www.oaic.gov.au" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">oaic.gov.au</a>.</p>

      <h2 id="third-parties"><span class="n">09</span>Third-party services</h2>
      <p>AccrualOS integrates with third-party tools such as Xero, MYOB, Karbon, Ignition, and others you choose to connect. Your use of those services is governed by their own privacy policies. We only access data from a connected service to the extent needed to provide the integration you enable.</p>

      <h2 id="children"><span class="n">10</span>Children’s privacy</h2>
      <p>AccrualOS is a business tool and is not directed to children. We do not knowingly collect personal information from anyone under 16.</p>

      <h2 id="changes"><span class="n">11</span>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. When we make material changes, we will update the "Last updated" date above and, where appropriate, notify you through the platform or by email.</p>

      <h2 id="contact"><span class="n">12</span>Contact us</h2>
      <p>If you have questions about this Privacy Policy or how we handle your information, please get in touch.</p>
      <div class="lg-contact">
        <h3>AccrualOS Privacy</h3>
        <p>Email: <a href="mailto:sales@sharktech.com.au">sales@sharktech.com.au</a></p>
        <p>Or use our <a href="/contact-us">contact form</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</main>
</Layout>
